| 14 | there is no exponent notation in numerals: `1e-5` is a `Syntax Error` | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | design limit (parser) | `basic/lexical-structure.tex`, "Numerals" | none | blinded | The error is the spec's own sentence, `a numeral contains letters and does not have a radix specifier`, logged by `validNumericLiteral` for any letter in a numeral without a radix specifier (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/nodes_util/NodeUtil.java:1158-1160` at c124c6b65). Workaround: a plain decimal numeral, `0.00001`. Probe `explorations/gap-ledger-probes/g06.fss`, in the parent of `e879b6a44`. |
| 177 | a mutable local needs its declared type: `p := loadParams(…)` with no prior declaration is `Variable p is not defined.`, and `var p = loadParams(…)` is `The type of p is required.` | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | implementation gap (parser) | `Specification-1.0-frozen/appendices/grammars/concrete-syntax.tex:1125-1128`, "Local Declarations" (`LocalVarDecl ::= [var] VarMayTypes = Expr \| [var] VarWTypes := Expr`); `:1135-1137` (`VarMayType ::= BindId [IsType]`) | none | run-c4 | The `var … =` half is the gap: `var p = e` is `VarMayTypes`, grammatical untyped, but `forLocalVarDeclOnly` refuses every mutable local without a type (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/parser_util/SyntaxChecker.java:179-181` at c124c6b65), with the `null` prefix of row 166. The `:=` half is the grammar's: `p := e` needs `VarWTypes`. Workaround: `var p: T = e`. It was the only annotation of Run C4's model that walk required (rows 176, 178, 131). Probe `explorations/run-c4/probes/types/E2` (`E` for the `:=` half), in the parent of `11bf69c39`. full text: history, row 177 |
| 251 | a tuple pattern in a parameter list is a `Syntax Error`: `f(g, (a, b, c): (Any, Any, Any))` does not parse, while the same function with a named tuple parameter destructured in the body does | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | design limit (parser) | `Specification-1.0-frozen/appendices/grammars/concrete-syntax.tex:712`, "Parameters" (`PlainParam ::= BindId [IsType]`: the specification has no destructuring parameter) | none | apl rung 5 | The error is `v01_tuple.fss:25:24: Syntax Error`, the column of the pattern's opening parenthesis; `explorations/apl/rung-5/v01_tuple.fss` keeps that form in a comment and runs the named spelling. Workaround: `aplEach(f, t: (Any,Any,Any)) = do (a, b, c) = t; … end`. Probe `explorations/apl/rung-5/v01_tuple.out.0`, in the parent of `1ee3b0bc5`. |
| 405 | a value parameter written without a type is refused on the compiled path wherever it appears, and under walk fails when its method implements an abstract declaration, so the specification's own `Cons` fails on both paths | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | implementation gap (checker) | silent | none | climb batch 5 rung S, its skeptic | siblings: 652. Compiled: `Missing parameter type for x`, for a function or method (`scala_src/typechecker/staticenv/STypeEnv.scala:200` at d4d454f9d) and for a local function where it is bound (`:72-75`); Appendix I's entry on a left-out parameter type states it. Walk runs a top-level function and a method implementing nothing; a method implementing an abstract declaration stops at its first call, generic or not, with an `InterpreterBug`, '... has neither body nor def instanceof Method'. `Cons` (`SpecData/examples/basic/Object.Decl.Cons.fss`) leaves `cons(x)` and `append(xs)` untyped. Workaround: type the parameters; then both paths print the answer. probe and full text: history, row 405 |
